        "text": "<thinking> To implement the requested files, I need to create the following Python files in the current working directory:\n\n1. upsert_document.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Firestore SDK to upsert a JSON document by its primary identifier.\n2. fetch_document.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Firestore SDK to fetch a document by identifier from a managed NoSQL store.\n3. query_documents.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Firestore SDK to query documents by a field value or partition-style key.\n4. conditional_update.py - This file will use the Google Cloud Firestore SDK to apply a conditional or version-aware update to one stored document.\n5. database_client.py - This file will provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Google Cloud Firestore.\n6. database_models.py - This file will define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Google Cloud Firestore.\n7. record_summary.py - This file will summarize retrieved document records.\n8. record_text_safety.py - This file will check user-generated document fields for unsafe content.\n9. record_translate.py - This file will translate user-facing document fields.\n10. record_export_archive.py - This file will archive exported document snapshots or attachments in managed object storage.\n\nI will start by creating the upsert_document.py file, which is the initial file requested by the user. </thinking>\n\n",
